nlining\n   - Advanced features: Generics (basic), Traits (basic), Pattern matching, Modules (basic), Macros (basic)\n   - Ecosystem integration: VSCode TextMate syntax highlighting, online Playground, Cargo.toml package system\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n   **Phase 1 Design Documents (Completed - 3,000+ lines):**\n   \n   - `docs/RUST_SUBSET_DESIGN.md` (1,000+ lines)\n     - Specifies 10 supported Rust features: basic types, variable declarations, functions, control flow, structs, arrays/vectors, ownership (basic), standard functions, error handling, type casting\n     - Documents unsupported features: advanced ownership/lifetimes, advanced types, advanced pattern matching, advanced generics/traits, macros, advanced modules, async programming\n     - Provides comprehensive examples of supported syntax\n     \n   - `docs/COMPILER_ARCHITECTURE.md` (1,000+ lines)\n     - Detailed 6-stage pipeline explanation with input/output for each stage\n     - Grammar rules in EBNF format\n     - 50+ token types defined\n     - AST node hierarchy documented\n     - Type compatibility rules explained\n     - Code generation patterns shown\n     - Example walkthrough of complete compilation process\n     \n   - `docs/IMPLEMENTATION_ROADMAP.md` (1,000+ lines)\n     - Phase-by-phase implementation schedule\n     - Detailed function signatures for each module\n     - Test strategy for each component\n     - Expected deliverables and line counts\n\n   **Phase 2 Compiler Implementation (Completed - 3,898 lines):**\n\n   - `src/tokenizer.jl` (555 lines)\n     - Implements MinRustTokenizer module\n     - Token enum with 60+ variants (keywords, operators, literals, punctuation)\n     - Tokenizer struct with position/line/column tracking\n     - Functions: tokenize(), scan_token(), scan_string!(), scan_char!(), scan_number!(), scan_identifier!()\n     - Keyword map with 34 keywords: fn, let, const, if, else, for, while, loop, match, struct, impl, trait, etc.\n     - Handles comments (