n     function parse_expression(parser::Parser)::Expr\n       return parse_assignment(parser)\n     end\n     \n     function parse_assignment(parser::Parser)::Expr\n       expr = parse_logical_or(parser)\n       if match_type(parser, ASSIGN)\n         advance!(parser)\n         right = parse_assignment(parser)\n         return BinaryOp(expr, \"=\", right)\n       end\n       return expr\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - `src/type_checker.jl` (1,000+ lines)\n     - Implements MinRustTypeChecker module\n     - TypeChecker struct with scope stack (vector of dicts), function table, error collection\n     - Key functions:\n       - check_types() - main entry point, calls collect_functions!() then check_item!() for each item\n       - Scope management: push_scope!(), pop_scope!(), declare_symbol!(), lookup_symbol()\n       - Type operations: types_equal(), is_compatible(), binary_op_result_type(), unary_op_result_type()\n       - Check functions: check_item!(), check_fn_decl!(), check_stmt!(), check_expr!()\n       - Expression type checking: check_literal(), check_identifier!(), check_binary_op!(), check_call!(), check_field_access!(), check_index!(), check_array_literal!()\n     - Implements full type inference for literals (Int→i32, Float→f64, String, char, bool)\n     - Binary operator validation (arithmetic requires same numeric types, comparisons return bool, etc.)\n     - Unary operator validation (-x for numeric, !x for bool, & creates reference, * dereferences)\n     - Function signature validation with argument type checking\n     - For-loop element type inference from iterable type\n     \n     Key pattern - type inference:\n     ```julia\n     function check_expr!(checker::TypeChecker, expr::Expr)::RustType\n       if isa(expr, Literal)\n         return check_literal(expr)\n       elseif isa(expr, Identifier)\n         return check_identifier!(checker, expr)\n       elseif isa(expr, BinaryOp)\n         return check_binary_op!(checker, expr)\n       # ... more expression types\n       end\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - `src/codegen.jl` (800 lines)\n     - Implements MinRustCodeGen module\n     - CodeGenerator struct with output buffer, variable counter, label counter, indent tracking\n     - Functions:\n       - generate_code() - main entry, generates #include directives, prototypes, implementations\n       - gen_fn_prototype() - outputs C function signature\n       - gen_fn_decl() - full function with body\n       - gen_struct_decl() - struct definition\n       - gen_block() - block statement execution\n       - gen_stmt() - statement dispatch to specific generators\n       - gen_var_decl(), gen_expr_stmt(), gen_if_stmt(), gen_for_stmt(), gen_while_stmt(), gen_loop_stmt(), gen_match_stmt(), gen_return_stmt()\n       - gen_expr() - expression evaluation (returns C code string)\n       - type_to_c() - Rust type to C type mapping (i32→int, f64→double, String→char*, &T→T*, etc.)\n     - Handles operator mapping to C equivalents\n     - Generates properly indented C code\n     - Uses temporary variable generation for complex expressions\n     \n     Key pattern - C code generation:\n     ```julia\n     function type_to_c(rust_type::RustType)::String\n       if isa(rust_type, PrimitiveType)\n         if rust_type.name == \"i32\"\n           return \"int\"\n         elseif rust_type.name == \"f64\"\n           return \"double\"\n         # ... more types\n         end\n       end\n     end\n     ```\n\n   - `src/compiler.jl` (300 lines)\n     - Implements MinRustCompiler module\n     - CompilationResult struct with success flag, C code, errors, token/AST node counts, warnings\n     - Main compile() function orchestrating full pipeline:\n       1. Tokenization (MinRustTokenizer.tokenize)\n       2. Parsing (MinRustParser.parse)\n       3. Type checking (MinRustTypeChecker.check_types)\n       4. Code generation (MinRustCodeGen.generate_code)\n       - Each step has try-catch error handling\n     - Helper function count_ast_nodes() for s